{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd","id":47274,"title":"B&S Kiasyd?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-11T23:57:24-08:00","id":47274,"title":"B&S Kiasyd?","content":"I would really like to see these guys done up, they are one of my favorite bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on how to go about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:22:39-08:00","id":47281,"title":"","content":"Oh shoot, I started working on an update to Mytherceria and I totally forgot! I have most of it done at this point, the 5th dot has been giving me a little trouble, but I'll at least post what I've got when I get back to my computer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T01:33:27-08:00","id":47294,"title":"","content":"Ya, the main problem with the discipline as written is that it actually has a lot of overlap with Auspex. I think it would be awesome to go a more fae inspired/mixed blood route or convert the version of the discipline from the second edition of &quot;Secrets of the Black hand&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:47:22-08:00","id":47406,"title":"","content":"Yeah, differentiating it from Auspex was a big part of the problem I was having. What I eventually decided to do was to give the Kiasyd Auspex and make Mytherica a series of bloodline-proprietary Auspex Devotions. Hopefully you can use that, I'm afraid I'm not really up to the task of designing a Discipline from scratch. I won't be able to post it until after 5:00, but I'll put it up as soon as I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:57:57-08:00","id":47480,"title":"","content":"Well, since I'm writing them as a direct Masquerade conversion for my own purposes, I wrote them as a Lasombra bloodline, with Auspex being the discipline they gain and Mytherceria being the unique set Auspex Devotions they can learn. But yes, for putting Kiasyd in Requiem, I would make them a Mekhet bloodline instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:28:08-08:00","id":47503,"title":"","content":"I think one of the characters in Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners (the bug man) was meant to be a reference to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T13:36:07-08:00","id":47582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make them a mehket bloodline. That solves the Auspex issue</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, this is a good idea. Auspex covers like three levels of the RAW Mythercia I really like Changeling Ward though, my Secrets of the Black Hand is packed up but I think that version dealt with more fae magic like having spikes shoot out of the ground and stuff but that is all I remember of it, is there a wiki or something of that version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T14:27:46-08:00","id":47610,"title":"","content":"Auspex and Dominate devotions really cover the majority of it very, very well. Even Changeling Ward (trance states, forgetting what direction to go, a nice application of low level Dominate for short term memory mixed with Auspex 3). Earth Swords and similar were from the old, OLD edition of the Sabbat Storytellers Guide, which had a much more direct &quot;Fae magic tricks&quot; angle; I forget if it was even 2nd edition at the time rather than 1st, with Bartholamew (sp?) and all that and the mini-adventure. <br /> <br /> Guide to the Sabbat Revised and on treated Mytherceria more with draining information, psychic vampirism (to a degree; memory etc. theft), mental confusion and the highest level where the strange alchemical cocktail of blood they had subsumed the vampiric aspects for a time letting them wander for a brief period as a human-ish individual. It's cleaner and makes more sense than the hodge-podge of its earlier edition predecessor, quite easy to port over though a good majority of it is basically an interesting Auspex redux. Changeling Ward and Riddle Phantastique are still pretty intact though, and the higher level things are... well, ugly, if not more disturbing subtly. You could conflate them with fae, abductions, missing time, lots of the eerier elements.<br /> <br /> They also lost Necromancy and instead had Dominate, Mytherceria and Obtenebration, though if this has changed in V20 I'm unsure. The old dark ages Libellus Sanguinus (if I remember right) references had them with Obtenebration Mytherceria and Potence. Their first incarnation gave them Necromancy, Mytherceria and Obtenebration.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you really want as Mekhet? Nos + Mekhet Clan Bane. Replace Celerity with Obtenebration. Add Dominate as the Fourth in-clan. Done. Given the Lasombra roots aren't really relevant anymore unless doing a hybrid game you could just as easily drop Obtenebration and replace it with something else that gives them some cool conceptual oomph. The Bug Man had Animalism (though that may be unrelated to Bloodline); looking at the new Animalism that'd be a pretty interesting addition Devotion wise to curse others, to blight crops and a few other fae-esque sorta angles without needing a custom Discipline.<br /> <br /> I've seen some fanmades that tried to bring back their first incarnations abilities by effectively giving them Fae Magic branches and more; likely could be dredged up if need be. Not my personal tastes, mind you; I preferred the direction they ended up going, vs the Fae/Vampire hybrid angle some fans went with with oodles of powers to basically mimic them.<br /> <br /> The Bug Man in Immortal Sinners is the Kiasyd you folks are referring too. There isn't a writeup on what his Bloodline entails beyond they suffered from both the Nosferatu and Mekhet clan weaknesses and he had pitch black eyes with a tendency to go into fugue states (much like abductions in a way with missing time etc.) at certain dates only to come back with little trinkets like human toes etc. The author used to post on the old forums and mentioned him; if they're around here, maybe they can provide some insight on where they wanted to go with the bloodline?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what Secrets of the Black Hand you're referring to; they were never printed in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and they certainly weren't in Caine's Chosen: The Black Hand that I remember either. You're likely looking at the material from the 1995 Storytellers Guide to the Sabbat; quite a bit out of date, though that's where Basilisk's Touch etc. was printed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T21:38:16-08:00","id":47900,"title":"","content":"Wow Tatterdemalion King, seems like you were thinking along pretty much the same lines as me. Here's my interpretation of Mytherceria.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Fae Sight (Auspex </b><b>\u00b7</b><b>)</b><br /> Where Auspex grants a Kiasyd enhanced perceptive powers, Mytherceria allows them to attune those senses to a more specialized purpose. Normally, Beast\u2019s Hackles only grants the vampire insight pertaining to immediate danger. With Fae Sight, the Kiasyd is able to use it to detect the presence of magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The Kiasyd must have successfully activated Beast\u2019s Hackles<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> None<br /> <br /> When the Kisayid with this Devotion uses Beast\u2019s Hackles, the player can ask a question that relate to magical energies within the area rather than danger. What follows is a list of sample questions that can be asked in place of those normally allowed by Beast\u2019s Hackles.<ul><li>Does anyone here know non-vampiric magic \u2013 and if I have seen it before, what kind?</li> <li>Has non-vampiric magic been used in this area recently \u2013 and if so, when?</li> <li>Has anyone here been to another realm (such as The Hedge, The Shadow, or The Astral realm) \u2013 and if I\u2019ve encountered someone who has been there before, which one?</li> </ul>This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Folderol (Auspex </b><b>\u00b7\u00b7</b><b>)</b><br /> One limitation of Uncanny Perception is the difficulty of using it to detect lies or misdirection. While some tricks can be employed, such as looking for emotions that do not match up with those a subject is presenting outwardly, it is far from reliable. Folderol solves that issue by actively detecting lies.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The Kiasyd must have successfully used Uncanny Perception against the subject during the scene<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Empathy + Auspex<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Kiasyd mistakes the truth for a lie, or a lie for the truth.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Kiasyd is unable to determine if the subject is lying.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Kiasyd knows if the subject\u2019s last statement was a lie. As with Uncanny Perception, this functions by allowing the Kiasyd\u2019s player to ask the storyteller a question, but the only question she can ask is \u201cis this person lying?\u201d<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As with a normal success, only the Kiasyd\u2019s player can ask \u201cis your character telling the whole truth?\u201d, effectively allowing her to detect lies of omission as well as outright falsehoods.<br /> This Devotion costs 1 Experience to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Aura Absorbtion (Auspex </b><b>\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7</b><b>)</b><br /> The Spirit\u2019s Touch allows Kindred to sense emotional impressions off of objects. With this Devotion, a Kiasyd can not only read those impressions, but absorb them, in much the same way the Fae harvest Glamour. As a vampire, the Kiasyd does not have the means to use those energies, but by absorbing them she does make it harder for other Kindred to read the object after her, as there is less of the emotion there to read.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The Kiasyd must have succeeded in using The Spirit\u2019s Touch on the object<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 night<br /> This power is used in conjunction with The Spirit\u2019s Touch. The Kiasyd imposes a penalty equal to the number of successes she rolled on The Spirit\u2019s Touch to any subsequent attempts to analyze the object with The Spirit\u2019s Touch (or similar aura sensing powers) for the rest of the night. If she scored an exceptional success, the psychic signature is not merely weakened \u2013 it is completely gone. Any questions the Kiasyd asked about the object cannot be asked about it again until the next sunrise, though anyone who attempts to ask is aware that there is nothing to learn, and does not \u201close\u201d the question.<br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Chanjelin Ward (Dominate </b><b>\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7</b><b>)</b><br /> The power of Dominate is normally used to command and control. The Kiasyd, on the other hand, can use it to bewilder and befuddle. The power of Entombed Command makes it possible to use subconscious triggers to activate the dominant\u2019s orders, and this Devotion makes use of that ability to burn a symbol into the back of the victim\u2019s mind. When the victim sees that symbol, he becomes disoriented.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Subterfuge + Dominate \u2013 victim\u2019s Resolve<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The Kiasyd must have inflicted the Mesmerized Condition on the victim.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One week per success, or one month per success (see below)<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Kiasyd\u2019s attempt to set up a trigger to confuse the victim backfires. The victim loses his Mesmerized Conditon, and for the next week, he gains the Steadfast Condition any time he sees the triggering symbol.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> For whatever reason, the symbol doesn\u2019t stick in the victim\u2019s mind. He is not affected one way or the other when he sees the symbol.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The vampire can implant a symbol in the victim\u2019s mind. For one week per success, or one month per success if the victim is in any stage of Vinculum towards the vampire, the victim gains the Confused Condition any time he sees the symbol.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As with a success, only the victim also gains the Lost Condition when he sees the symbol.<br /> This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>The Riddle Phantastique (Auspex </b><b>\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7</b><b>)</b><br /> The power of Auspex eventually allows Kindred to Lay Open the Mind of a victim learning his secrets, as well as implanting thoughts or ideas into his head. The Riddle Phantastique allows a Kiyasid to use that ability to implant a particularly insidious idea \u2013 A riddle, puzzle, or enigma that the victim cannot help but obsess over until he solves it.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The Kiasyd must have already succeeded in using Lay Open the Mind on the victim during the scene<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Occult + Auspex \u2013 Resolve + Blood Potency<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The victim\u2019s mind rejects the Kiasyd. The effects of Lay Open the Mind end prematurely.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The victim dismisses the riddle as an unimportant curiosity.<br /> <b>Success:</b> After successfully breaking into a victim\u2019s thoughts with Lay Open the Mind, the Kiasyd can focus to plant a riddle in his head instead of dragging up an unpleasant memory. This causes the Obsession Condition. The Kiasyd can end the Condition prematurely by telling him the answer, but unless she does, the only way the victim can resolve the Condition is by solving the riddle. Doing so is an extended Wits + Occult roll with a target number of successes equal to three times the Kiasyd\u2019s successes. Each roll represents an hour of doing nothing but ponder the riddle. The victim can roll a number of times equal to his unmodified dice pool. If the victim rolls a dramatic failure and opts to abandon the action, or runs out of rolls without solving the riddle, he can take one point of Lethal damage to start over.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As with a success, except that the riddle nags at the victim\u2019s consciousness so incessantly that he suffers from the Distracted Condition whenever he is not actively trying to solve the riddle.<br /> A victim can only be subject to one use of The Riddle Phantastique at a time.<br /> This Devotion costs 3 Experiences to learn.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously, Kiasyd would be a Mekhet Bloodline with Dominate. I haven't written them up yet, but I'll post that when it's done. Sorry it took so long, I hope you can make some use of it, even if it is a little more focused on emulating the V20 version than on being a Fae-style discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T21:52:10-08:00","id":47916,"title":"","content":"Ya, I meant the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> I like your write up Charlaquin but I think it is just to similar to Auspex or Dominate. How would bloodline get access to Dominate? I definitely see them as having Auspex, Obfuscate, and Celerity. I am not sure where you would fit in Dominate and Mytherceria. <br /> <br /> Here is a write up I found online and I really like the first three levels, the next three could use a little work. <br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mytherceria:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mytherceria is the manifestation of <a href=\"http://everything2.com/title/fae\" target=\"_blank\">fae</a> blood and glamour in the Kaisyd blood. It confers abilities related to the fae, madness, and insight. Mytherceria is as much a passive Discipline as an Active one, conferring benefits across the board.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>* Fae Sight:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This power allows the Kaisyd to perceive that which lies on the other side of the obfuscating shroud of disbelief that clouds the minds of the living and the dead alike. The Vampire's Fae nature is strong enough that his perception pierces dimly into the faery realms. The vampire may recognize any fae <a href=\"http://everything2.com/title/masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">masquerading</a> as human, although he cannot detect their presence in <a href=\"http://everything2.com/title/Arcadia\" target=\"_blank\">Arcadia</a>, and more importantly, the Kaisyd can feel the presence of hobgoblins, imps, and other entities responsible for the fortunes of mortals and kindred alike. Although the Kaisyd cannot actually see these creatures, he can instinctually react to their presence. This ultimately boils down to a sixth sense concerning unfortunate events about to take place, such as a car having a blowout, a gun misfiring (or accidentally firing) or a person likely to meet their end. This perception manifests as a sense of dread or foreboding concerning a particular object or person and does not reveal in any explicit manner what will happen in the future.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This power also allows a Kaisyd to perceive other supernatural occurrences, including other vampires using astral projection, the presence of wraiths, or be aware when his mind is being read.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> -</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> This power is considered always on, the vampire may add his Mytherceria dots to any dice pool or defense score for resisting mind-clouding effects such as Obfuscate or some Nightmare abilities (but not Dominate) or to detect supernatural presences or events, such as having his mind read, or perceiving a vampire in astral form spying on him. This power is commonly added to Auspex dice pools, but is only useful for perceiving things of supernatural origin (Auras are inherent to all beings, and as such this ability does not affect Aura perception. Also an individual hiding without the aid of Obfuscate is not any easier to see with this power, but one using Obfuscate way very well give himself, or his object of choice, away in situations in which the Kaisyd may not have found them were they mundanely hidden). The Storyteller has the last word on what counts as supernatural and what doesn't.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This power is what makes it possible for the Kaisyd to Aid the Ordo Dracul in &quot;Finding the Wyrm's Nests&quot; and is responsible for their myriad eccentricities.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Note that, although this power has wide-ranging applications, it's usefulness is tied to the Discipline's level, and as such the effects will be minimal at first and increase over time, gained insights should be proportional to the Discipline's level according to the chart. Note that effects listed below are cumulative.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">* Bad feelings about objects, places, or people.<br /> ** Instincts are directed mildly by desire and help the Kaisyd to solve problems or riddles.<br /> *** Specific premonitions that are accurate to the spirit of an event, but usually not literally.<br /> **** Small bits of information about important places, items, and people appear randomly.<br /> ***** The Kindred knows when he's being lied to.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>** Darkling Trickery</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At this level of insight the Kaisyd is able to enact &quot;Pranks&quot; of relatively benign natures. The nature of this is that of the fae themselves, evident, but unbelievable. This power is used most often to confuse or disorient enemies or rivals. Its effects vary widely, should never be capable of inflicting more than one bashing damage total, and should always manifest in some completely implausible manner. Examples include a targets hair turning suddenly white, a plant changing colors or becoming animated (though it could not perform any task), milk curdling, disembodied voices, frogs coming out of a drain, or some other equally disturbing but benign effect. Let your imagination go wild.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keep in mind that these effects may often seem funny when known to be false, but are deeply disturbing, despite their whimsical nature, when they appear before someone.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The effects of this power have caused some to call into question whether there is some relationship between the Kaisyd and the Malkovian bloodline of the Ventrue. When asked, the Kaisyd respond &quot;That's ridiculous,&quot; but in practice there seems to be some unspoken affinity between the two bloodlines.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 blood</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> The Kaisyd rolls Wits + Occult + Mytherceria vs. Subject's Composure + <a href=\"http://everything2.com/title/Blood+Potency\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Potency</a> (If the ability targets someone directly).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Action:</b> Contested, resistance is reflexive.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Roll Results:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anyone who witnesses (or experiences, as the case may be) the effect must make a Composure + Blood Potency roll at a -3 penalty to avoid &quot;Freaking Out.&quot; Effects with longer durations or particularly disturbing effects may require multiple composure rolls or higher penalties to those rolls. This effect does not induce frenzy of any kind by virtue of it's own power, although the effect itself may do so under some circumstances.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dramatic Failure: Some aspect (or the polar opposite of some aspect when necessary) of the intended effect manifests toward the kindred himself for the scene. In general this isn't too terrible a thing as effects are mostly benign, although it is likely that it will impair the vampire's social rolls in some way. Examples include the kindred's own hair turning white, a flower sprouting from his ear and regrouping instantly whenever it is cut off, vomiting up curdled milk, hearing voices (causes distraction penalties), or gaining a long sticky tongue that renders him incapable of speech, and which he compulsively extends out of his mouth every few seconds (although it could not confer any benefits). These are also good ideas for things to do to enemies.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1 success Two Turns<br /> 2 successes Five Turns<br /> 3 successes 20 turns (1 minute)<br /> 4 successes 10 minutes<br /> 5+ successes 1 hour or scene</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">All effects &quot;clean themselves up&quot; when their duration is exhausted or the Kaisyd chooses to end them. Hair regains its natural color, plants return to normal, disembodied voices become quiet, or spontaneously generated frogs hurriedly dissipate and disappear once out of sight. Note that effects always end in some subtle manner. Frogs will not blink out of existence, and hair will regain its color when the subject is away from a mirror. Even if the effect is in full, unadulterated view, a mild obfuscating effect will cause the ability's cessation to be un-spectacular. Some effects, such as curdling milk, do not end at all.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>*** Diamond Soul</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At this level, the Kaisyd's duel nature as Vampire and Fae confers the benefits of glamour upon the kindred.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> -</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> The Kaisyd may add dice equal to his Mytherceria to all Blood Potency dice pools and defense scores for resisting supernatural effects. This does not stack with the level-one effect, which confers a greater bonus to resistances involving supernatural subterfuge.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Action:</b> N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Example: A Kaisyd with Mytherceria 3 and Blood Potency 2 is faced with the Nightmare Level 1 ability &quot;Monstrous Countenance.&quot; His soak pool is equal to his Composure + Blood Potency + Mytherceria instead of just Composure + Blood Potency.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>**** Faery Wards</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Vampire has to protect his property. This power allows the Kindred to manipulate the addling nature of unbelief and Fae Glamour. By inscribing a boggling and impossible design or image onto a surface the kindred can cause all who see it to become disoriented, distracted, and confused. The image itself may appear to move, look back at the viewer, or simply be incomprehensible. This power cannot be avoided by simply looking away once the ward has been seen; knowledge of its presence is enough to sustain the effect. Kaisyd often inscribe their books containing more valuable or sensitive information with these wards. Kaisyd are immune to their own wards.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 willpower point</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Crafts + Mytherceria - 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Action:</b> Extended</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Roll Results:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The player must declare the desired number of successes before he begins rolling, because an image cannot be left unfinished simply because the player decides that he has enough successes. An unfinished image holds no enchantment. Successes may be accumulated as long as the Kaisyd is able to remain in one place, relatively undistracted, and work on the image. Each roll represents 30 minutes of drawing, etching, or otherwise marking a surface. Once he target number of successes is reached the ward is finished and no further rolls may be made to improve it.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dramatic Failure: The vampire becomes involved in the enchantment of creating the ward and will continue doing so unaware for the remainder of the scene or until attacked. If attacked, all actions taken until end of scene are at a -3 penalty. The ward contains no enchantment.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure: If a failure is rolled on any roll the ward is accidentally ruined. The image has an obvious flaw and holds no enchantment. All accumulated successes are lost and the surface must be cleaned or a new surface used to make a new attempt.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Success: Any person who sees the ward must make a Composure + Blood Potency roll and beat the Kaisyd's successes in creating the ward to avoid becoming disoriented.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If the ward is in a confusing or non-descript locale (labyrinthine hallways or dark forest) the victim becomes hopelessly disoriented and lost, returning to the location of the ward again and again until he has accumulated 3X the ward's creation successes on an extended Resolve + Composure roll made once every 30 minutes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If the ward is in a location where it is impossible to get lost, such as a normal house or building, or on an object, such as a book or safe, then the subject will be unable to concentrate in the presence of the ward and thus incapable of memorizing or even understanding anything written in a book, or of breaking a safe, or any other task requiring moderate concentration. A book may, however, be taken from the room and read elsewhere, and so it is wise to mark more prized possessions directly.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Three successes are required to create a ward. The Ward lasts for the following durations.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">3 Successes One day<br /> 4 Successes Two days<br /> 5 Successes One Week<br /> 6 Successes One Month<br /> 7 Successes Six Months<br /> 8 Successes One Year</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>***** The Dreaming</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">At this level the Kaisyd may journey into The Dreaming, or the Chimerical Realm. The Dreaming is the realm of Arcadia closest to the Mortal world. Dreaming realms are connected to the mortal world in two ways: the first is at the location of the dreamer herself, and the second is at the location on earth where the dream itself takes place. Furthermore, Dreaming realms are connected to each other by &quot;real world&quot; location, subject, and atmosphere. The Dreaming is a very real place where fantastic and impossible things can and do happen. The world is subject to dream logic, but the dangers are physically real to one actually inside of The Dreaming. As an existing realm, certain static objects, events, and even characters can exist there, and many objects from the mortal realm have found themselves physically transported there by the Fae. Any Fae met in this realm will likely be very upset to find a vampire there.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Dreaming is composed of the dreams of mortals, and as such is a widely varying place. Nightmares are very common, as are endless alleys, sadistic torturers, absurd creatures, jilted lovers, deep wishes and fantasies, dark secrets, discordant architecture, and deep darkness. Kindred must remain savvy as to their surroundings, as dreams take place in both the night and the day, and a Chimerical Sun is just as dangerous to kindred, as it is a manifestation of the real sun. Kindred should have little difficulty isolating themselves to dreams taking place at night, or with no aspect of time at all, but beware emerging from dreams haphazardly, as a single mortal taking a nap at midday in China could provide the unfortunate end to a Kaisyd in America.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Entering the dream of a particular mortal (or supernatural creature capable of sleep) may provide a way to learn their secrets, or to torment them. Killing someone in their dream, presuming that they are not present physically in The Dreaming, but are rather dreaming themselves, results in the target losing two willpower and waking up immediately.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In general, the Dreaming is a rather persistent place. Archetypal dreams are shared by myriads of mortals, and are sustained even as individuals rise and fall to Hypno's embrace. Individual and personal dreams, however, end when the dreamer awakes. A Kaisyd in a dream that ends has plenty of time to move to another if the dreamer is waking, but if the dreamer awakes suddenly, or is awakened from within the dream the vampire is shunted either to another dream, or to the mortal realm. This can be dangerous, and vampires are advised to avoid disturbing the dreamers to directly.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dreams are also often incomplete worlds. It is possible to run around the back of a prominent building in a dreamscape only to find a gaping abyss where loading bays should be. The dreamer has never wandered behind this building in the mortal realm and has not considered what may be there, and as such it is not included in her dream.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Leaving the Dreaming requires that the Kaisyd return to his point of entry. He may instead find some other suitable symbolic place of departure and expend a willpower point to manifest it as an exit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower and 1 Blood</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence + Occult + Mytherceria - target's Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Kaisyd may enter the dreaming in one of two ways: he may imbibe one blood point from a sleeper and expend that blood point along with a willpower to enter the sleeper's dreams. The vampire will fade from the kiss' ecstasy to the dream itself.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Alternatively the Kaisyd may attempt to enter the Dreaming directly. This action is performed with a -5 penalty. The Vampire must draw a door (or other dream-appropriate portal) in blood, or draw a glyph in blood on an existing transition point. Points may include doors, tapestries that may be pulled aside, windows, or even cliffs or other jumping-off points. Regardless, some physical transition between the mortal world and The Dreaming is necessary.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Roll Results:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dramatic Failure: The Vampire is shunted into a deep nightmare, or some hellish and dangerous realm of his own creation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure: Nothing happens. A vampire who has used a cliff as a transition point falls to the ground, potentially harming himself. One who uses a door simply enters the next room.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Success: The Kaisyd enters the Dreaming as expected.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exceptional Success: The kindred enters the Dreaming and maintains a sense of the surroundings of the sleeper or location at which he entered, and may leave at will without having to search for an exit.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T22:44:05-08:00","id":47940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=47916#post47916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya, I meant the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I like your write up Charlaquin but I think it is just to similar to Auspex or Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it's a series of Devotions for Auspex and Dominate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=47916#post47916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would bloodline get access to Dominate? I definitely see them as having Auspex, Obfuscate, and Celerity. I am not sure where you would fit in Dominate and Mytherceria.</div> </div> </div> </div>They get Auspex, Obfuscate, and Celerity by being Mekhet, obviously. The bloodline gives them Dominate. That's all of the Disciplines they have, no need to fit in Mytherceria because it isn't a Discipline in and of itself. It's is a series of single-Discipline Devotions, specific to the bloodline, that allows them to modify their Auspex and Dominate to see magic, sense lies, absorb auras, create wards, and confound people with riddles. Think like the Nelapsi from Bloodlines: The Hidden. They were a Daeva bloodline with Nightmare, but they also had a set of Devotions that were unique to the Nelapsi (even though neither of their Disciplines were actually unique).<br /> Anyway, sorry if my take was not quite what you were looking for. For what it's worth, I do eventually plan to eventually make Devotions to cover Darkling Trick and Goblinism as well, but they are not my current priority as I still haven't finished converting all of the core Disciplines. But if you're still interested I will let you know when I get to that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T22:56:44-08:00","id":47950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=47940#post47940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because it's a series of Devotions for Auspex and Dominate.<br /> <br /> <br /> They get Auspex, Obfuscate, and Celerity by being Mekhet, obviously. The bloodline gives them Dominate. That's all of the Disciplines they have, no need to fit in Mytherceria because it isn't a Discipline in and of itself. It's is a series of single-Discipline Devotions, specific to the bloodline, that allows them to modify their Auspex and Dominate to see magic, sense lies, absorb auras, create wards, and confound people with riddles. Think like the Nelapsi from Bloodlines: The Hidden. They were a Daeva bloodline with Nightmare, but they also had a set of Devotions that were unique to the Nelapsi (even though neither of their Disciplines were actually unique).<br /> Anyway, sorry if my take was not quite what you were looking for. For what it's worth, I do eventually plan to eventually make Devotions to cover Darkling Trick and Goblinism as well, but they are not my current priority as I still haven't finished converting all of the core Disciplines. But if you're still interested I will let you know when I get to that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I like it. I am now confused. So, they get Dominate as their bloodline Discipline which makes sense and is fine. I do not get how their devotions work, do those devotions replace those levels of Dominate and Auspex when you buy that dot instead of the RAW?<br /> <br /> What would their weakness be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T01:18:50-08:00","id":48009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=47950#post47950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, I like it. I am now confused. So, they get Dominate as their bloodline Discipline which makes sense and is fine. I do not get how their devotions work, do those devotions replace those levels of Dominate and Auspex when you buy that dot instead of the RAW? What would their weakness be?</div> </div> </div> </div> They work just like any other Devotions. They have a particular level of a particular Discipline as a prerequisite. If you have that prerequisite, you can pay the experience cost of the Devotion to learn it, and then you just that power. Now, way I designed these particular Devotions, they all either enhance or function very similarly to a specific level of a specific Discipline, so that might be what's causing the confusion. If that is the case I probably need to work on the formatting to make that all a bit clearer. For example, The Riddle Phantastique is a Devotion with the prerequisite Discipline Auspex 4, and costs. 3 experiences to learn. It gives you a power that can only be activated after successfully using Lay Open the Mind, and allows you to inflict a Condition with very specific criteria for resolution on the same victim. Does that make a little more sense? Honestly I'm not sure where I'm losing you, and I want to make sure I wrote these Devotions in a way that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T07:40:39-08:00","id":48158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=48009#post48009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They work just like any other Devotions. They have a particular level of a particular Discipline as a prerequisite. If you have that prerequisite, you can pay the experience cost of the Devotion to learn it, and then you just that power. Now, way I designed these particular Devotions, they all either enhance or function very similarly to a specific level of a specific Discipline, so that might be what's causing the confusion. If that is the case I probably need to work on the formatting to make that all a bit clearer. For example, The Riddle Phantastique is a Devotion with the prerequisite Discipline Auspex 4, and costs. 3 experiences to learn. It gives you a power that can only be activated after successfully using Lay Open the Mind, and allows you to inflict a Condition with very specific criteria for resolution on the same victim. Does that make a little more sense? Honestly I'm not sure where I'm losing you, and I want to make sure I wrote these Devotions in a way that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ok, I got it. Thank you. I am curious what back story would you use for them in VtR? Would you go the Fae route or something else?<br /> <br /> I guess we could just tack on the Nos weakness, but I guess it depends on what angle we take with origin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:14:13-08:00","id":48330,"title":"","content":"Well like I said, I'm actually converting for a game of Masquerade with nWoD rules. So my version would technically be a Bloodline of Lasombra that gains Auspex as their Bloodline Discipline and use the fluff from Masquerade as-written. But if I were to transfer them to the Requiem setting, I would make them a Mekhet bloodline with Dominate as their bloodline Discipline, and probably alter the fluff slightly. What might be cool is to play on the Mekhet's scholarly angle. Maybe the bloodline's progenitor was a Mekhet who lost his mind researching the Fae. Maybe he found a way to use Twilight Projection to enter dreams, or even the hedge (which would actually make another great Mytherceria Devotion - requires Auspex 5 and works the same way, but lets you project your consciousness into the Astral or the Hedge instead of Twilight) and came back changed. Alternatively, he could have beeb a Changeling or even a fetch that was embraced by a Mekhet. But that's both less exciting and raises a lot of awkward questions like if other supernats can be embraced... So yeah, I'd definitely go with the former. Might write up that Devotion when I have time, but as I said I have other priorities at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T11:15:19-08:00","id":48332,"title":"","content":"As for the weakness, I would just give them the Aversion Bane for iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T12:35:52-08:00","id":48402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=48158#post48158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah ok, I got it. Thank you. I am curious what back story would you use for them in VtR? Would you go the Fae route or something else?<br /> <br /> I guess we could just tack on the Nos weakness, but I guess it depends on what angle we take with origin</div> </div> </div> </div>You could assume Marconius accidentally found a keyed portal to the Hedge and developed his bloodline while trying to get out. Maybe feeding off hobs or changelings or somesuch","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T17:44:05-08:00","id":48615,"title":"","content":"I'd lay their creation firmly at the hands of the Ordo Dracul; alchemical experimentation with the blood of &quot;Tzeernebooch&quot; or what have you and fae blood and what not? Look at the Nossie fella in the Nos Clanbook and elsewhere. Toss a smattering of clandestine fae experiments mixed with the blood of some... thing, lets call it a Hidden One (see Nossies again!) and the result wasn't some new Scale or understanding, but a &quot;volunteer&quot; becoming very, very strange indeed. Toss in their academic proclivities and it's a fairly good mix to explain their Bloodline culture being what it is (make their origin Victorian era for extra fun; see the old Victorian Era Vampire and the &quot;Scarlets&quot;).<br /> <br /> Hell, if you really want to, make them the strange result of Marconius progressively experimenting with strange Vitae on himself to somehow force change in the vampire state rather than as a guinea pig; bit by bit he got stranger and stranger taking an approach that some in the Ordo certainly weren't very approving of (publicly). Hell, some might even cast doubt that they're &quot;proper Kindred&quot; any more, vs some aberration like the other vampires out there to add a little tension and a reason for them to not be a common sight. Even getting Marconius the boot from the Ordo potentially.<br /> <br /> That way a lot of the academic angles make sense as less of some badly contrived obsession &quot;yeah, and so since you're Kiasyd you read a lot and don't do much. Because. You're a clone of...er wait, why are we even being presented again?&quot; so much as the society they form and what that society values. Individually they should run the gamut of concepts beyond &quot;haven-bound bookworm&quot;. Some just keep by the Research and Development angle to see what their new state is -really- capable of; or perhaps a way to remedy it or trace back those blood sources used and go investigating places few in the right mind would consider sane; like the Hedge, Arcadia, the Underworld or similar.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think taking extra damage from Iron is a bit too watered down; it should have a more profound effect if its kept in place. Otherwise it's a flaw likely to never come up (who the hell, really, is going to figure out a Mekhet Bloodline has a cold iron sensitivity if it only hurts them more? Let alone by accident?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 01-13-2014, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T19:11:24-08:00","id":48653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=48615#post48615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think taking extra damage from Iron is a bit too watered down; it should have a more profound effect if its kept in place. Otherwise it's a flaw likely to never come up (who the hell, really, is going to figure out a Mekhet Bloodline has a cold iron sensitivity if it only hurts them more? Let alone by accident?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, when I said &quot;the aversion bane to iron&quot; I meant the Repulsion Bane, as in the one from B&amp;S, and I meant any iron, not just cold iron. (That does leave some questions about steel or other alloys that contain Iron, but I'd just say they don't contain a high enough concentration of Iron to count). That Bane doesn't only hurt more, it makes it so they can't come within [10 - humanity] feet of it without spending a point of Willpower, and also deals the same amount of damage (bashing) if it enters an open wound. I'd say that's a fairly reasonable bloodline bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-13-2014, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T20:33:34-08:00","id":48690,"title":"","content":"That'd make quite a bit more sense to me, I'd go with it as a Bloodline Bane with little issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T05:12:14-08:00","id":48882,"title":"","content":"I like your Mytherceria devotions, Charlaquin! (even if Aura Absorption duration should be increased to make it actually useful IMO)<br /> <br /> What kind of alloy would count? I'd say wrought iron. Very little carbon and it's not used much anymore, but there is a lot of old stuff still around if you know where to look. Like the Eiffel Tower...<br /> <br /> Some of the old banes from Danse Macabre, like Lunar illumination, sound very appropriate for a Kyasid, if not strong enough taken alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T07:27:03-08:00","id":48941,"title":"","content":"Yeah, wrought iron would probably count. Honestly, I don't know squat about metallurgy, so I would be a poor judge. Only reason I excluded steel is because it's freaking everywhere in modern society, you wouldn't be able to go a block without running out if willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T18:36:07-08:00","id":49428,"title":"","content":"Kiasyd and cold iron is a topic of great confusion usually. Cold iron is untempered, &quot;pure&quot; iron, and is incredibly hard to come by these days. Extending the bane slightly to alloys and tempered iron would be good to maintain the bane as something less situational like the VtM version had.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of the Kiasyd as a transcendental experiment by the Ordo. Having a Kiasyd Occult Hunter in VtR would be pretty damn cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T00:23:15-08:00","id":50497,"title":"","content":"Ya, I am really liking what everyone has come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T05:41:49-08:00","id":50596,"title":"","content":"I've kinda gotten bitten by the Kiasyd bug a bit from this; I prefer keeping things &quot;fresher&quot; if that makes sense in Requiem than too much re-use of V:tM (with some exceptions; the Tzimisce saw a return as a sister/brother Bloodline of another homebrew in the game I co-run), but way, -way- back when I really had a thing for Kiasyd. Looking now at the Banes system, Bug Man, the new Ordo Dracul, the Auspex updates and more I'm kind wanting to use them once again. It wouldn't be the first time alchemical experimentation yielded an odd bloodline; look at the Azerkatil from Ordo Dracul for instance.<br /> <br /> On another note; if one takes a nod from the Neglatu, given they've got some really interesting alterations to base Kindred considerations, what possible &quot;Mostly standard Kindred template, with some tweaks&quot; options would be interesting? Some Devotions I'd still love being around, but if we were to take the route where there's some fundamental tweaks to to their vampiric state like that new Bloodline, how would we do it?<br /> <br /> Would they be some funky types really tied to the otherwordly? Would their Kindred senses also encompass Fae-things or something else inborn? Would they be able to access doors to the Hedge? Would these guys and gals be cast-outs of the Ordo, but taken in by say, the Bloody Mary Covenant, perhaps even founders? Are they vampires that feed off blood but, taking the revised angle... also part Mnemovore, feasting on memories, thoughts and dreams of others? That last one to me has some -big- potential. I'd love to see them as something weirder, more insidious than many realize. Missing time. Alien appearances. Fae ties. Breeding experiments. Hidden Ones. The Ordo Dracul. Experimental Scales reliant on supernatural blood.<br /> <br /> There's a funky thread going through there. If doing crossover, they may be a threat in certain Changeling circles. In others, their creation may have in part had silent benefactors among the Autumn Court for the blood used, who in turn were very interested in the end results. Or was it a Gentry getting involved, subdued and used for it?<br /> <br /> Was the fae-related things just one component among others just as relevant; was Marconius a Mnemovore that was experimented upon? Are the Kiasyd actually the cause of them (think Revenants; except the ones made by Kiasyd are those)?<br /> <br /> Or did it all start &quot;innocently&quot; enough and over time Marconius and his offspring just got stranger, and stranger? Less of an &quot;uplifting&quot; and more of a degeneration, or, more honestly, a shift towards something that may almost be pushing to a new &quot;Clan&quot; of sorts bit by bit the more they've had contact with strange vitae, the more they've experimented. They're redefining vampirism alright; they're just becoming a different sort of one that's not quite the standard blood-sucker bit by bit.<br /> <br /> This is something of a brain-storming request; how would you folks do some mutations/changes to them to reflect their twisted alchemical, fae and who knows what alterations that didn't directly rely on Disciplines and Devotions? Personally, I wouldn't mind playing up that, sure, there's -some- Fae blood to them, but it's more than that. The whole Nossie &quot;Hidden Ones&quot; really, -really- springs to mind to me with them for some reason given Tzeernebooch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 01-16-2014, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T11:57:58-08:00","id":50906,"title":"","content":"There's also the possibility that they're not a bloodline, but a type of non-kindred vampire, like the Kui-Jin. Maybe a type of blood drinking goblin that came from the hedge, and as with the others have slowly become more and more like the Kindred by sharing their blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T18:00:33-08:00","id":51240,"title":"","content":"Wow, now you have me thinking Kiasyd as a clan....a fae oriented type of clan..<br /> <br /> I am thinking of turning Mythercia into a fae magic type of thing, here is just off of the top of my head...<br /> <br /> * Fae Sight?<br /> <br /> ** Darkling Trickery<br /> <br /> *** Changeling Ward<br /> <br /> **** Earth Spikes (or whatever its called<br /> <br /> ***** Basalisks Touch<br /> <br /> Don't really have an idea on the mechanics...but ya I think this looks kinda awesome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":1227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","user":"Shenron","date":". 01-17-2014, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T00:16:32-08:00","id":59584,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T03:10:14-08:00","id":784033,"title":"","content":"I found this <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Vampire_the_Requiem_Homebrew_Bloodlines#Kiasyd:_The_Weirdlings\" target=\"_blank\">link</a> when looking for &quot;Kiasyd Requiem&quot; on google. I'm adapting some things.<br /> I thinking about creating a homebrew Kiasyd from the Mekhet clan. With Domite as their 4th discipline and Mytheceria as a Blood Sorcery. (Kinda like the Architets of the Monolith)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T06:32:17-08:00","id":784701,"title":"","content":"I'd go with feeding off of people's integrity, knowledge, and identity. Make it a Mekhet bloodline with Dominate as the bonus discipline. Let it feed on certain parts of the person's life kind of like how Demons take aspects for cover. Imo, Kiasyd need to be able to make Not!Lost.<br /> <br /> Make it convert one of the Mekhet's existing banes to a Repulsion to Cold Iron. If the Mekhet has no Banes, their first bane becomes a repulsion to Cold Iron. In addition, make them lose Humanity at regular intervals and have to take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:34:42-08:00","id":785678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=47406#post47406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, differentiating it from Auspex was a big part of the problem I was having. What I eventually decided to do was to give the Kiasyd Auspex and make Mytherica a series of bloodline-proprietary Auspex Devotions. Hopefully you can use that, I'm afraid I'm not really up to the task of designing a Discipline from scratch. I won't be able to post it until after 5:00, but I'll put it up as soon as I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever thought of simply making it as Auspex devotions tweaked/tainted in some way by their bloodline weakness? It kind of worked for the Khaibit update, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T19:03:42-08:00","id":785690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=785678#post785678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever thought of simply making it as Auspex devotions tweaked/tainted in some way by their bloodline weakness? It kind of worked for the Khaibit update, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is a pretty old thread. I don't think there were any 2e Bloodlines at the time I wrote those Devotions. Maybe Neglatu, but I know Khaibit weren't around yet. If I were to take another crack at it, it would probably look pretty different from that draft, now that I've had more time to acclimate to 2e's design style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:12:56-08:00","id":785734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=785690#post785690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this is a pretty old thread. I don't think there were any 2e Bloodlines at the time I wrote those Devotions. Maybe Neglatu, but I know Khaibit weren't around yet. If I were to take another crack at it, it would probably look pretty different from that draft, now that I've had more time to acclimate to 2e's design style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Khaibit were adapted pretty early too, but you're right, my bad, wasn't pay due attention to the date of the first posts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T21:47:14-08:00","id":785753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/47274-b-s-kiasyd?p=785734#post785734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Khaibit were adapted pretty early too, but you're right, my bad, wasn't pay due attention to the date of the first posts...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no worries. I was just saying I think I would build it more like the Khaibit or the Kerberoi if I re-wrote it now, but at that time I didn't consider it cause I didn't have anything to compare to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T10:17:32-08:00","id":786064,"title":"","content":"I really like the Bug Man nod to the Kiasyd in Night Horrors. If I were to do an Elizabethan Requiem game, I would totally do the bloodline there, because of all the connections with Changelings going on. I was even thinking of a GoT Bloodraven-like character (as at his prime younger days) as a recurring antagonist/ally.<br /> <br /> Something like Mekhet or Nosferatu, gain the weakness of the other clan upon joining. Eyes go fully black. Perhaps the other clan main discipline as well (Auspex or Nightmare. A couple of thematic devotions would be cool as well. Probably in Elizabethan era they have huge ties to Cr\u00faac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T06:29:19-08:00","id":787316,"title":"","content":"I made a PDF of them. But it is in Portuguese(BR), I'm planning on translate it to English in a couple days.<br /> Here's the link: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0Bxnrkdt3S6o0cTU1Mk9jMzhVVXc\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0Bx...TU1Mk9jMzhVVXc</a><br /> Any feedback would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B2